+# Merge of the DS41 and GLM TP3 lines (2026-11-13)
+
+> Commit ids shown as [unpublished] belong to the local history before the 2026-11-14 port and are not in the public repository.
+
+Branch `tp3-merge` (worktree `~/flare-up-main`), local only, not pushed.
+
+## Sides
+
+| Side | Ref | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| first parent (DS41) | `ds41-tp3-sync` @ [unpublished] | code behind the live DS41 default package 1241 (upstream cbf21a12 + 88 commits) |
+| second parent (GLM) | `glm-hyperflare` @ [unpublished] | internal history of the published GLM release |
+| merge base | [unpublished] | `ds41-tp3-sync` minus its last commit |
+
+Why [unpublished] and not the published squash ac9136b0:
+
+- [unpublished] descends from cbf21a12, and its history already contains the DS41 sync line up to [unpublished] (the GLM
+  sync merged it, [unpublished]). The real merge base is therefore [unpublished], and the DS41 side adds only one commit
+  ([unpublished], tuning scratch preference).
+- `git diff [unpublished] ac9136b0` covers 18 files, and every change is a path scrub for publication
+  (`/m2-2/flare-ckpt` -> `/path/to/ckpt`, home paths -> `$HOME`, drive names). No code differs. The private
+  branch keeps the real paths, as the DS41 side does.
+- Merging ac9136b0 (base cbf21a12, both sides carrying the DS41 TP3 work) gave 14 conflicts. Merging [unpublished]
+  gives 1 conflict, and both histories stay intact.
+
+## Conflict resolutions
+
+| File | DS41 side ([unpublished]) | GLM side ([unpublished]) | Kept |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `ignition/preparation/tuning.py` (import) | imports `scratch_preference.from_environment` | imports `COMPILE_HEADROOM_BYTES` from `host_memory` (upstream [unpublished], compile headroom as a preparation setting) | both imports |
+| `tuning.py`, `RecordedPreparationSession.__init__` | after `headroom_bytes` validation: reads the scratch preference and calls the b12x `configure_scratch_preference` (warns and falls back if the venv lacks the patch) | after `headroom_bytes`: validates and stores `compile_headroom_bytes` | both, compile headroom first, then the scratch preference. The two are independent |
+| `tuning.py`, tuning report dict | `"scratch_preference": identity or None` | `"compile_headroom_bytes": ...` | both keys |
+
+## Auto-merged files checked for semantic clashes
+
+The DS41 side changed only `ignition/preparation/{collectives,scratch_preference,tuning}.py`,
+`tests/preparation/test_scratch_preference.py` and `tp3-patches/flashinfer-tuning-scratch-preference.patch`. The GLM
+side did not touch any of these except `tuning.py` (resolved above). As a result, every other file in the merged
+tree is byte-identical to [unpublished]. The tree differs from [unpublished] only in those 5 DS41 files and the test fix below.
+
+GLM-side changes since [unpublished] that reach DS41 code paths. All of them are already in the GLM release binary
+and venv code:
+
+- `deepseek41/{bootstrap,recipe}.py`: plumbing for `compile_headroom_bytes` only (default 8 GiB, which equals the
+  old constant `_HEADROOM_BYTES`).
+- `tuning.py`: `_prepare_compiler_toolchain()` now runs at import (upstream [unpublished]) instead of per session.
+- `components/weights.py`: additive `pad=` loader path (GLM TP3 padding). The default keyword sets are unchanged.
+- `components/vision_staging.py`: additive (packed-layout helpers for the GLM lean tower). The DS41 staging code
+  is unchanged.
+- `components/linear.py` `BatchedUnquantizedProjection`: cuBLAS vs Triton race (upstream PR #231). Only GLM MLA
+  and kimi31 use it, not DS41.
+- Helios/Heliopause (13 files vs [unpublished]): core cache payload linking and work queue (export I/O, upstream),
+  catalog/packing accept a partial last page (DCP3 768-token pages), and GLM tool-argument retention
+  (`output/tagged.rs` `parameter_value`, which only `argument_tags.rs` = GLM uses). DS41 uses `chatml.rs`, which is unchanged.
+  The merged Rust is identical to the binaries in `~/flare-up-glm-sync` ([unpublished]) and `~/flare-up-glm-tp2-sync`
+  ([unpublished]), which serve the GLM packages today.
+
+**Behaviour change for GLM exports:** the scratch preference is on by default (`FLARE_TUNE_SCRATCH_TOLERANCE` default
+0.02) and now applies to GLM exports too. The GLM packages 130000 and 130307 were exported without it (the GLM venv
+lacks the b12x patch). To reproduce them, export with `FLARE_TUNE_SCRATCH_TOLERANCE=0`. With 0 the selection keys
+and choices are the unpatched ones. A GLM export at 0.02 or 0.05 is a separate KV/speed experiment.
+
+## Extra commit
+
+[unpublished] `test_declarations`: the GLM three-rank DCP test's `prepare_group` stub still used the `package_storage`
+keyword. Upstream renamed it to `core_storage`. This was a pre-existing failure on [unpublished] and now passes.
+
+## CPU test results
+
+Suite: `tests/recipes/test_deepseek41*.py tests/recipes/test_glm53*.py tests/recipes/test_declarations.py
+tests/components tests/preparation`, run with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=` and `PYTHONPATH=<tree>` on the shared sync
+venv. Each parent ran in a throwaway detached worktree. The results were compared per test (junit XML).
+
+| Tree | passed | failed | skipped |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| [unpublished] (DS41) | 2674 | 66 | 1803 |
+| [unpublished] (GLM) | 2946 | 67 | 1922 |
+| merged before the test fix | 2959 | 67 | 1922 |
+| merged ([unpublished]) | 2960 | 66 | 1922 |
+
+- The merged branch has no failure that is new against both parents, and no test that passes in a parent fails here.
+- The 66 remaining failures are the same 66 that fail on [unpublished]. They come from the environment: template patches
+  that fetch from the Hub, the native recipe contract library, packaging, runtime_triton, and the qwen/kimi
+  declaration cases.
+- 27 test ids exist only on [unpublished] because GLM-side tests were renamed or reparametrized
+  (`test_glm53_speculative` with `reuse`, `test_glm53_mla_cuda`/`test_glm53_weights` ids). The merged tree carries
+  the GLM versions.
+
+Helios `cargo test --lib --features server,runtime-core`: merged 1374 passed / 4 failed and [unpublished] 1357 / 4,
+with the same 4 failures (template-dir tests: `frontend::jinja` x2, `frontend::templates`, `native_prompt_tests`).
+The 17 extra tests come from the GLM side (TTFT guard boundary/policy tests, protocol and argument-tag tests).
+
+## Build and environment
+
+- `cargo build --release` in `flare-cli/` succeeded in 57 s (`-j 16`, nice 10).
+- `flare run --help` is identical for the merged binary and the sync, glm-sync and glm-tp2-sync binaries: 67
+  flags each.
+- `.venv` is a symlink to the sync venv (FlashInfer 0.7.3 + tp3-patches including the scratch-preference patch). The
+  GLM worktrees use the glm-sync venv. That venv is identical to the sync venv except for this patch
+  (`b12x/preparation/{session,types}.py`).
+- `.brrr-ext` was copied from `~/flare-up-sync`.
+- `.b12x-overlay` was built from the sync venv with `tp3-tools/make-b12x-overlay.sh`. The world-3 pull-gather patch
+  applies cleanly on top of the scratch-preference patch. Rebuild it after any venv change.
+- Exports must set `PYTHONPATH=<this worktree>`. Without it the venv's editable `ignition` resolves to
+  `~/flare-up-sync`.
+
